`OutlinedInput` passes an `inputRef` prop to any custom `inputComponent`. `TextareaAutosize` expects its ref as React’s `ref`, so it forwards `inputRef` to the native `<textarea>` and React warns.

Use an adapter that translates the prop:

```jsx
const AutosizeInput = React.forwardRef(function AutosizeInput(props, ref) {
  const { inputRef, ...other } = props;

  return <TextareaAutosize {...other} ref={inputRef || ref} />;
});

<OutlinedInput inputComponent={AutosizeInput} />
```

Or, if you only need an autosizing multiline MUI input, avoid `inputComponent` entirely:

```jsx
<OutlinedInput multiline minRows={3} />
```

`OutlinedInput` already renders its compatible autosizing textarea when `multiline` is enabled. [OutlinedInput API](https://mui.com/material-ui/api/outlined-input/)
